EXT. ROOFTOP CRICKET PITCH - MUMBAI - DAWN

A concrete rooftop between apartment towers. Wire fencing. Laundry flapping. Chai steam. A mat taped to the cement. Wickets spray-painted on a water tank.

FARRUKH SHAIKH, 28, captain, clutches a battered bat. CASPIAN MOURA, 17, rookie bowler, scuffs a tennis ball on his shirt. A tall woman in a sari, NEW COACH, 40s, stands at the edge of the mat with a clipboard and no expression.

FARRUKH
Rookie. Let's see it.

CASPIAN
Now?

FARRUKH
Now.

Caspian jogs in, delivers. The ball smacks the mat, rises off a crack, and clips the water tank with a bang. Farrukh doesn't flinch.

FARRUKH (CONT'D)
Again.

Caspian bowls. Farrukh swings, misses. The ball slams the tank again.

NEW COACH
(flat)
Your grip is open.

CASPIAN
Sorry, Ma'am?

NEW COACH
Close your hand. Where I can't see daylight between your fingers.

Caspian closes his fingers around the ball. Bowls. Farrukh swings. Connects. The ball sails off the roof, over the wire, into the morning haze.

FARRUKH
(whispering)
Who's she?

CASPIAN
She says she's our coach.

FARRUKH
Whose coach?

NEW COACH
Ibarra. Rosa Ibarra.

FARRUKH
Ibarra? As in the Ibarra? From the 2011 final?

IBARRA
I do not discuss 2011.

CASPIAN
You played in 2011?

IBARRA
Another.

She sets the clipboard on the water tank. Takes the ball from Caspian. Rolls it across the mat to Farrukh.

IBARRA (CONT'D)
Captain. Show me what you do with the next one.

Farrukh looks at the ball. At Caspian. At the horizon where the first one landed.

FARRUKH
(low)
That's the last ball we have.

IBARRA
Then play it well.
